<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augusto B. Leguía</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1863–1932</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Augusto Bernardino Leguía</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augusto B. Leguía was a Peruvian businessman and politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1908 to 1912 and again from 1919 to 1930. His second rule, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oncenio">Oncenio</a>, began with a coup, centralised power and financed roads, ports and public works in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> with heavy borrowing in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and it settled border disputes with Chile and Colombia. He was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luis-sanchez-cerro">Luis Sánchez Cerro</a> in 1930 and died in prison in 1932.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augusto-b-leguia.jpg" alt="Augusto B. Leguía" width="320" height="548" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Peru (Life time: ca. 1908-1912) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Augusto_B._Legu%C3%ADa_(portrait).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
